## What happened — 2026-01-05, closing session

**Regime:** Bull market — SPY 687.72 above both the 50-day (679.1) and 200-day (628.1) MAs, near its 52-week high, VIX 14.9. Bar raised to **8.0**.

**Six analysts ran in parallel** (all prices verified point-in-time via `price-fetch` as_of 2026-01-05):

| Agent | Pick | Final | Fate |
|---|---|---|---|
| quant | AMZN | 0.00 | **Debate PASS** |
| catalyst | STZ | 7.40 | Below 8.0 (reduced) |
| macro | XLE | 6.26 | Below bar |
| sentiment | NKE | 6.18 | Below bar |
| contrarian | TTD | 4.36 | Falling knife |
| crypto | IREN | 3.93 | Parabolic chase (0.7x fund) |

**The debate gate decided the day:**
- **AMZN** — Bear exposed an omitted **RSI 83.6** and the total absence of any datable catalyst in the 15-day window (Q4 earnings is Feb 5; CES is soft only). The bull *conceded both* → 2 unrebutted serious weaknesses → PASS.
- **STZ** — The bull did valuable forensic work, **factually rebutting** the bear's central claim (STZ actually *rose* +2.3% / +1.0% day-after its Q1/Q2 beats; the declines came from the separate Sep 2 guide-cut). But no evidence the Hispanic-consumer headwind had stabilized → one unrebutted weakness + an aggressive +8% target → reduced-size **7.40 < 8.0**.

**Decision: PASS.** No pick cleared the bull-market bar. Per closing-session rules, excess capital swept to **SPY** (13 sh @ 687.72 = $8,940.36) — the disciplined outcome of holding the index when nothing beats it.

Two findings worth flagging for the learning loop: (1) the AMZN pick is a clean example of a momentum writeup that hides its own exhaustion signal (RSI) and names no catalyst — exactly what the narrative/debate layers exist to catch; (2) the STZ bull's catch — verifying the bear's empirical premise with point-in-time prices rather than rebutting its tone — shows the debate adding real value beyond just skepticism.
